# Credentials

Check where you run first: `test -n "$OP_CONNECT_HOST" && echo imp || echo local`. In both places, never
echo a token or a secret value.

## Local PC (1Password, scoped tokens per repo)

- Use the Linux `op` CLI with a service-account token that `op-mint` scopes to one profile's vaults.
- Each repo has its own profile and its own vault, both named after the repo. The profile's token
  lives in `~/projects/<repo>/.claude/settings.local.json`, which overrides the global
  `~/.claude/settings.json`. `op-mint --list` gives every profile, its vaults and its settings file.
- These profiles differ from the convention:
  - `global` uses the `zgeoff` vault, in `~/.claude/settings.json`. `zgeoff` holds the items every
    agent shares, such as `repo-sync-github-app`.
  - `imp` uses the `imp-e2e` vault, which holds imp's e2e tailnet OAuth client.
  - `vers` adds `vers-ci` (read-only), which holds only what the vers infra-drift CI job reads.
  - `cloud` adds `cloud-deploy`, which holds the secrets cloud's deploy workflows read, and `imp`,
    where cloud stores the files service's agent token.
  - `orchestrator` reads across several repos' vaults, and its settings file sits outside every repo.
- My personal vaults are reachable only through `op-win`, with my approval.
- Claude Code loads the token from `env.OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN`, so plain `op item get …` works
  there. Any other agent (or a Claude session started before a re-mint) reads it inline:
  `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN=$(jq -r .env.OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN <settings file>) op …`.
- Tokens expire ~7d. When an `op` call fails auth, re-mint with `op-mint <profile>` (dotfiles
  `~/.local/bin/op-mint`; `op-mint --list` shows the profiles). Don't ask me to sign in the Linux CLI;
  `op-mint` mints through `op-win`, which reaches my Windows 1Password app; approving may need a tap.
  A new profile or vault means editing `op-mint`, not minting by hand.
- Each mint makes a new `claude-<profile>-<date>` service account — prune stale ones in the
  1Password web UI occasionally.

## Cloud (imp)

- No `op-mint`, `op-win` or service-account token exists here. Don't look for one.
- `op read op://imp/<item>/<field>` works through 1Password Connect, for the `imp` vault only.
- Brokered APIs need no key in the guest: the host adds the credential on the way out. Today that
  covers GitHub and the model gateways; call them directly.
- If a secret you need isn't reachable, report the gap. Never ask me to paste a secret into the
  session.

